#
# Module
#
ModuleFreeMobileSmsName = Free Mobile SMS
ModuleFreeMobileSmsDesc = Send SMS notifications to your own Free Mobile lines
FreeMobileSmsDescription = Send SMS notifications to your own Free Mobile lines
FreeMobileSmsDescriptionLong = SMS sending engine using the Free Mobile notification API (free with a Free Mobile plan). The API only sends SMS to the line that owns the login, so each recipient must be one of the lines declared in the setup. Choose it in Setup > SMS.

#
# Setup
#
FreeMobileSmsSetup = Free Mobile SMS setup
FreeMobileSmsSetupHelp = Enable the option "Notifications par SMS" in your Free Mobile subscriber area (Mes Options) to get the login and the identification key of each line.
FreeMobileSmsWarningNotSendMode = Free Mobile is not the SMS sending method yet: choose "freemobilesms" in %s.
FreeMobileSmsInfoTest = Free Mobile is the SMS sending method. You can send a test SMS from %s.
FreeMobileSmsAccounts = Lines
FreeMobileSmsNumber = Phone number
FreeMobileSmsNumberHelp = Number of the Free Mobile line. SMS sent to this number use the login and key of this row.
FreeMobileSmsLogin = Login
FreeMobileSmsLoginHelp = Login of the Free Mobile subscriber area (8 digits)
FreeMobileSmsApiKey = Identification key
FreeMobileSmsApiKeyHelp = Key generated by Free Mobile when enabling SMS notifications. It is stored encrypted and never displayed again.
FreeMobileSmsApiKeyStored = Key stored
FreeMobileSmsTemplate = SMS template
FreeMobileSmsTemplateHelp = Text sent around each message: __SMS_MESSAGE__ is replaced by the message. Standard substitution variables like __MYCOMPANY_NAME__ can be used. Without __SMS_MESSAGE__, messages are sent unchanged.
FreeMobileSmsExampleMessage = Reminder: meeting tomorrow at 10:00
FreeMobileSmsErrorAccountFields = Phone number, login and key are required
FreeMobileSmsErrorBadNumber = The phone number %s is not valid
FreeMobileSmsErrorAccountExists = A line with number %s already exists

#
# Sending
#
FreeMobileSmsErrorUnknownNumber = Free Mobile can only send SMS to the lines of its setup, and %s is not one of them
FreeMobileSmsError400 = Free Mobile: a mandatory parameter is missing
FreeMobileSmsError402 = Free Mobile: too many SMS sent in too short a time, try again later
FreeMobileSmsError403 = Free Mobile: the service is not enabled in the subscriber area, or the login / key is wrong
FreeMobileSmsError500 = Free Mobile: server error, try again later
FreeMobileSmsErrorHttp = Free Mobile: unexpected answer (HTTP %s) %s
